Groups organized by sexuality, age, and/or gender identity.

For schedules ', null, null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('XybNN39fTlquRKw5Bwnx8g', 'Asexual/Aromantic Umbrella Mormons Online Community', 'Online Community', null, '{}'::text[], array['Asexual']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f663c89dc4ac15aa61147df_novo-logo-afirma_o_n.png', 'An online community by Affirmation. For those within the asexual or aromantic umbrella.', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/130720233784404/', null, false, null, null),
  ('idG9YJCGSFy1Mbb7jNfxFw', 'Ben There, Done That', 'Blog', null, '{}'::text[], array['LDS']::text[], 'https://storage.googleapis.com/glide-prod.appspot.com/uploads-v2/NSfaaNV0fRhAK9yZqEUi/pub/GOYdUbtbqiUsCSb70KcL.png', '"Questions from the Closet" Co-Host Ben Schilaty''s personal blog. He discusses his journey of staying active in the church and broadly sharing his life story as a gay Mormon.', 'benschilaty.blogspot.com', null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('LTHYCav1RKa.N41aFE4wlg', 'Bi/Pan Adults Friendship Circle', 'Support Circles', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County','Utah County','Washington County']::text[], array['Bi/Pansexual']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/Encircle_Logo.png', 'This friendship circle is for adults (18+) who identify as bisexual or pansexual. 

Friendship Circles?
These groups are designed to provide a connection with folx you identify with and help you manage the trials you encounter every day. Friendship Circles create an opportunity for you to take control and thrive in your own life.

Friendship Circles provide opportunities for sharing, connection, and support through discussion of issues and experiences relevant to each group, often exploring the intersectionality of conservative cultures, spirituality, sexuality, social issues, transitional issues, and health issues and the ways it impacts us. The groups also provide a great support network—members in similar circumstances with similar feelings with whom they can share in an open and unedited fashion.

Groups organized by sexuality, age, and/or gender identity.

For schedules and more inf', null, null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('itZMhomnTdS3yZMeahr.wQ', 'BW Bastian Foundation', 'Business', null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f563d9be36f1b167826fa82_5f356c7856e21ab3badfc63b_BW_20Bastian.png', 'The B.W. Bastian Foundation strives to build community and understanding by supporting local and national institutions. Financial support is directed to the Arts through educational outreach. A strong commitment is placed on programs and organizations that benefit, encourage, and preserve the rights of individuals, promote equality for the LGBTQ+ community and HIV/AIDS programs. The B.W. Bastian Foundation only supports organizations who wholeheartedly embrace the principle of equality. As such, each organization must include a statement specifically stating their commitment to equality for all Americans, including the gay and lesbian community, in their application.', 'bastianfoundation.org', null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('bxyxcGmkSES3tSvhUSG9LA', 'BYU USGA', 'Other', null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f5637d8c04fcd0094f27b14_5f2d99dcfeb406f686539c20_USGA.jpeg', 'Welcome to USGA! 

Understanding Sexuality, Gender, and Allyship (USGA) is an unofficial group of Brigham Young University students, faculty, and guests who wish to enhance the BYU community by providing a safe space for open, respectful conversation on LGBTQ & SSA topics. USGA is a place of refuge and our priority is to have compassion and to seek understanding through listening. Harassment or antagonism against any person or organization will not be tolerated. Members are asked to be mindful of USGA’s political neutrality and to be respectful of BYU, The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints, and the beliefs and experiences of others. In order to maintain a safe and welcoming environment, USGA supports its members in upholding the Honor Code, and expects all participants to be respectful of others’ names, pronouns, and identities. They encourage all not to make assumptions or ask', 'www.usgabyu.com', null, 'byu.usga@gmail.com', '1230 Bulldog Ave. Provo, UT 84604', 'https://www.facebook.com/UsgaAtByu/', null, true, null, null),
  ('YflgqyezRr-Hp3.MgLuANA', 'Cache Pride Center', 'Pride Center', 'Cache County', array['Cache County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f5633d7e36f1b64ac26e98c_5f358fc72b040487de0d14ba_Cache_20Pride.jpeg', 'Cache Pride Center is a program of the Cache Valley Unitarian Universalists Church and is committed to transforming and supporting Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual, Transgender, Queer, Pansexual, plus (LGBTQIAP+) Cache Valley communities through support groups, comprehensive programming, suicide prevention, mentoring, community advocacy, and community training devised to promote positive outlooks and changes within underserved populations. 

- Groups: Cache Pride Center has groups/programs for preteens, teens, transgender individuals, & LGBTQ+ adults.
- Parent Support: We know it is important for LGBTQ+ persons to have support. Cache Pride Center offers parent support group services
- We offer have other services for those in need of food, clothing, hygiene items, and temporary housing/shelter. 
- We assist in finding health care and mental health professionals.', 'cachepridecenter.org', null, 'info@cachepridecenter.org', '596 E 900 N, Logan, UT 84321', 'https://www.facebook.com/CachePrideCenter/', null, true, null, null),
  ('ym.DNrDaTFGdcpMYPnJi8w', 'CDC National Info Hotline', 'Wellness/Medical', null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f5638fbca15840081e624c4_5f2e1292de355b3d44088f9a_CDC-Logo20Edited.jpeg', 'CDC’s national health information hotline provides answers to your questions regarding HIV, how to protect yourself, and where to get an HIV test. In English, en Español, 8 am to 8 pm ET, Monday through Friday.', null, '1-888-232-6348', null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('wRpZolU.RYa7.8LL4j8NQg', 'Celebrate Therapy', 'Mental Health/Counseling', 'Utah County', array['Utah County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://storage.googleapis.com/glide-prod.appspot.com/uploads-v2/GLyS34gJTOtHtpGe05Cl/pub/kJF0rI9AnP2lEf9CYEfG.png', 'Celebrate Therapy is the first clinic in Provo, Utah and the surrounding area that is owned and run by a team of queer clinicians. We work to support clients in becoming confident and supported in their own queerness. We’ll also work alongside family members who are working through how to support their queer loved ones. We are hoping to lead a transformational change Utah County and beyond!', 'https://www.celebratetherapy.org/', '(801) 448-7712', null, '286 W. Center St, Provo, UT 84601', null, 'https://www.instagram.com/celebratetherapy/', true, null, null),
  ('n7PV3lEJRLOwkHZx5X49Qw', 'Cheer Salt Lake', 'Social Groups', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://storage.googleapis.com/glide-prod.appspot.com/uploads-v2/GLyS34gJTOtHtpGe05Cl/pub/3rAsggbnYrS9JNUYX1pe.png', 'Founded in 2011, Cheer Salt Lake raises funds and awareness for those living with life-challenging conditions in the LGBTQ community and beyond. We''re an inclusive team that welcomes volunteers from all backgrounds and partners with a variety of community organizations in Salt Lake, Provo, and Ogden. We''re a federal 501(c)3 non-profit and registered charity in the state of Utah.', 'cheersaltlake.org', '(415) 745-0923', 'info@cheersaltlake.org', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/cheersaltlake/', 'https://www.instagram.com/cheersaltlake/', true, null, null),
  ('cwTKvQXGTPeQXY81zyYLZg', 'Children''s Service Society of Utah', 'Professional Services', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], array['Families/Youth']::text[], 'https://storage.googleapis.com/glide-prod.appspot.com/uploads-v2/vZEd46xUe6vz0E68sGvW/pub/khGexBFNlQHEJrkPEYeh.png', 'Children’s Service Society of Utah empowers families and caregivers through services that support the safety and well-being of children. CSS is the oldest non-denominational child welfare and family support agency in Utah. Through the years Children’s Service Society has evolved its programs according to the needs of the children and families they serve in the community. Today Children’s Service Society of Utah empowers families and caregivers through services that support the safety and well-being of children. This is accomplished through these programs: Adoption, Grandfamilies Kinship Care, Care About Childcare and Utah Parents in Action, Home Visitation.', 'cssutah.org', '801-355-7444', null, '655 East 4500 South, Suite 200', 'https://www.facebook.com/ChildrensServiceSociety', 'https://www.instagram.com/cssutah/', true, null, null),
  ('xwkyEW5LTH2fCtNfl2H-Tg', 'Cougar Pride', 'College Resources', 'Utah County', array['Utah County']::text[], array['LGBTQ Adult']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/6205d999787f5a57c61009ba_a16184fe-a0be-400b-af1e-8217e8dde010.png', 'Cougar Pride Center aims to empower queer BYU students, celebrate progress, and advocate for change through collaborative activism. Founded in 2021, we are a volunteer-run organization that strives to create community and care for LGBTQ+ individuals on campus.', 'cougarpridecenter.org', null, 'cougarpridecenter@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/cougarpridecenter', 'instagram.com/cougarpridecenter', true, null, null),
  ('7pp3DPUvSEKGajNY2s2KNA', 'Creating Community - LGBTQ & Allies', 'FHE/Sunday Service', 'Davis County', array['Davis County']::text[], array['LDS']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/6178b3b8a19f8b75c14f01be_Copy_of_Copy_of_Unnamed_Design.png', 'A space for LGBTQ people and their loved ones. We are here to share a connection, friendship, and support. We have a get-together on the fourth Sunday of each month in Davis County, Utah.', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/1492727134249314/', null, false, null, null),
  ('4mhrIN0DSJyuTPUo2tuBfA', 'Damn These Heels', 'Publications/Media', null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5fac1405b22c78f75bed23ec_Damn_these_heels.jpg', 'The annual film festival explores LGBTQ issues, ideas, and art through showcasing dramatic and documentary films from around the world. Damn These Heels remains a community focused, grassroots, locally-produced festival with strong community partnerships.', 'https://www.utahfilmcenter.org/', null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('M780wDVXRTCbahEP3GXBUw', 'Dixie State LGBTQ+ Resource Center', 'College Resources', 'Washington County', array['Washington County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5fb1a52fdc2686a1709f58b6_Dixie_State_GSA.jpg', 'Our mission is to promote understanding and acceptance for all individuals by education, activities, and service for the campus and larger community. The club provides support and social networking for all persuasions of people. We want to raise awareness about suicide rates and promote education of homosexuality and acceptance for equality in Saint George.

WHAT WE DO

The Resource Center empowers the LGBTQ+ people who are part of DSU’s community. Much of this comes from the simple act of providing information to everyone. Other parts of the center’s mission include scholarships, mentoring, promoting visibility and acceptance, and outreach. We create a space for students where they feel safe to gather, express themselves, discuss ideas, learn, and teach others. We work as a team to improve LGBTQ+ inclusion across campus.

- Education
- Safe Zone Training
- Mentoring Support
- Peer Suppo', 'https://lgbt.dixie.edu/', '435-652-7752', 'lgbtq@dixie.edu', '261 S 900 E #207, St. George, UT 84770', 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/dixiegsa/', null, true, null, null),
  ('cmtjNgreRdWFk--O4vXK0g', 'Dragon Dads', 'Other', null, '{}'::text[], array['Parent']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f563220c13ff61101bfe559_5f2e131ed336660bfd9a8e26_Dragon_20Dads.png', 'We fight to prevent teen suicide and to provide support and education to other fathers who want to show love and support for their LGBTQIA+ children.If you would like more information or would like to join, please click below to begin the process.', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/dragondads/', null, false, null, null),
  ('Zvd.MoggSMeqRU76qbZg9g', 'Emmaus LGBTQ Ministry', 'Online Community', null, '{}'::text[], array['LDS','Allies']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/351855910_643312370634812_3848817731976547444_n.png', 'Emmaus fosters and supports ministry to and with LGBTQ individuals and their families in and adjacent to The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints.

Emmaus is a community of heterosexual/cisgender and LGBTQ Latter-day Saints who are called to ministry for the safety, well-being and happiness of LGBTQ people in and adjacent to The Church of Jesus Christ.

We envision communities, congregations and families where LGBTQ individuals know they are cherished, where they are free from discrimination and inequality, where they are fully heard, understood and protected, and where their agency is respected.

We feel driven to do this work by our testimonies of the Gospel. We know there is a place in Christ’s Church and in our Heavenly Parents’ plan for every single one of us, and our hearts ache for the anguish caused by misunderstanding and lack of knowledge.

We believe that the way forwar', 'emmauslgbtq.org', null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/emmauslgbtq/', null, false, null, null),
  ('cJ00BaioRA-VPJPA8I.JGg', 'Encircle Provo', 'Pride Center', 'Utah County', array['Utah County']::text[], array['Youth']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/60fae9494cd60f1a5fb4331d_218384456_867797794136825_712167177273530856_n.png', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('I.DpcfncSs-2oEGxiJF4ag', 'Encircle Salt Lake', 'Pride Center', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], array['Youth']::text[], 'https://storage.googleapis.com/glide-prod.appspot.com/uploads-v2/NSfaaNV0fRhAK9yZqEUi/pub/JxMoQgrgY2YkgVnpnB07.png', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('8nnixaVnSF-hsPNkuwt2dA', 'Encircle St. George', 'Pride Center', 'Washington County', array['Washington County']::text[], array['Youth']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/60fae9a7d3f1f71629a45f99_219479815_878659989722201_322750248107661649_n.png', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('gpE2VUOtRGmhtpKu8RBEXA', 'Equality Utah', 'Education/Advocacy', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5fb96adfcdd292cdcc7806c5_Equality_utah.png', 'Equality Utah works to build a community where every Utahn is valued for being who they are regardless of sexual orientation or gender identity. We believe everyone in our state deserves to be treated with respect and understanding and to be afforded the same basic freedoms and opportunities as everyone else.

OUR VISION: A fair and just Utah. OUR MISSION: To secure equal rights and protections for lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender and queer Utahns and their families.

OUR ISSUES: 
Nondiscrimination
LGBTQ Families
Victim Targeting
LGBTQ Youth
Transgender Utahns
Suicide Prevention', 'equalityutah.org', '801-355-3479', 'info@equalityutah.org', '175 200 S #1004, Salt Lake City, UT 84101', 'https://www.facebook.com/EqualityUtah', 'https://www.instagram.com/equalityutah/', true, null, null),
  ('m800StjxS4qBVsDklvyXAw', 'Family Acceptance Project', 'Research', null, '{}'::text[], array['Parent']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f693891f8dc32460437cc17_Untitled_design_(2).png', 'The Family Acceptance Project® is a research, intervention, education and policy initiative that works to prevent health and mental health risks for lesbian, gay, bisexual and transgender (LGBTQ) children and youth, including suicide, homelessness, drug use and HIV – in the context of their families, cultures and faith communities. We use a research-based, culturally grounded approach to help ethnically, racially and religiously diverse families learn to support their LGBTQ children.Our team has put research into practice by developing an evidence-based family model of wellness, prevention and care to strengthen families and promote positive development and healthy futures for LGBTQ children and youth. We provide training and consultation on our family-based prevention and intervention approach across the United States and in other countries.', 'familyproject.sfsu.edu', null, 'fap@sfsu.edu', null, null, null, true, null, null),
  ('5XGNcHPvQ8atsvA5n5OFkw', 'Family Solutions Counseling', 'Mental Health/Counseling', 'Cache County', array['Cache County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/6173206ad2718886817d3532_66262393_411908376084012_2964773000525643776_n.png', 'LGBTQIAP+ ALLIED

Supporting you

As a practice that focuses on being inclusive and affirmative to the LGBTQIAP+ community, we have created this resource page with you in mind. While all of our therapists are accepting of LGBTQIAP+, those with particular experience and ability to be affirmative are listed here.

Autumn Abbott, MSWI

Beth Allred, CSW

Robin Hunt, LCSW

Rachel White, CSW

Evelyn Tovar, CSW-I

Skyler Taylor, CSW

Stacie Later, CSW

Lauren Harrigian, ACMH

Proud member of the LGBTQ-Affirmative Psychotherapist Guild of Utah Inc.', 'familysolutionsutah.org', '435-799-5035', 'info@familysolutionsutah.org', '115 Golf Course Road Suite E Logan,UT 84321', 'https://www.facebook.com/familysolutionsutah/', null, true, null, null),
  ('rYQDtR8EQCCv6ffZRcPsgg', 'Fathers in Affirmation Online Community', 'Online Community', null, '{}'::text[], array['Parent']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f663c89dc4ac15aa61147df_novo-logo-afirma_o_n.png', 'For those who are gay fathers or would be fathers.', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/470473746493580/', null, false, null, null),
  ('2.u53pD-QE-tRWNskcclLQ', 'FHE for All Cache Valley', 'FHE/Sunday Service', 'Cache County', array['Cache County']::text[], array['LDS']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f564238b0505c3613b7d071_Untitled_design_(1).png', 'A gathering of friends, family and individuals with ties to the LGBTQ community where we meet monthly to share in fellowship, song, and refreshment- FHE style. Our goal is to affirm faith and facilitate space for healing and encouragement for ALL: Allies, LGBTQ and Leaders of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints here in Cache Valley. For information and access, please contact Jenny Mathews or Sue Hendricks below.', null, null, null, null, null, 'https://instagram.com/fheforall_cachevalley?igshid=1hjkd3qn298x3', false, null, null),
  ('zkWUDnDPTnS2fxG3GbQxRw', 'First Step House', 'Mental Health/Counseling', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://storage.googleapis.com/glide-prod.appspot.com/uploads-v2/vZEd46xUe6vz0E68sGvW/pub/DRDsngDiPDfs3mEHc9zx.png', 'We offer a suite of patient-centered and evidenced-based programs that span a continuum of care across pre-treatment, treatment entry, recovery initiation, housing, employment, and long-term recovery management.', 'https://firststephouse.org', '801-359-8862 ext. 2129', null, '440 E. 500 S Salt Lake City, Utah 84102', 'https://www.facebook.com/firststephouse', null, true, null, null),
  ('eSeMeX7zQWCzbnQOytWJDw', 'Flourish Therapy', 'Mental Health/Counseling', 'Utah County', array['Utah County','Davis County','Salt Lake County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5fa5e1cd79f25bc54ed2dd82_cropped-Copy-of-Flourish-Icon.png', 'Flourish Therapy is a 501(c)(3) non -profit organization that provides subsidized therapy for LGBTQ clients and offers a wide variety of therapy options including: individual, couples, family and group counseling for all age groups, including short- and long-term counseling, crisis intervention, parent intervention, and support services with a focus on quality care for LGBTQ clients and their families. They finance more than 100 free sessions a month and 75% of their clients pay less than $50.00 per session. The clinical staff includes culturally competent licensed mental health practitioners, marriage and family therapists and counselors. Flourish works with several insurances, including Select Health, PEHP, EMI and DMBA. Flourish Therapy is based in Utah county, with therapy services offered across, Utah, Davis, and Salt Lake counties.', 'flourishtherapy.org', '385-309-1038', 'info@flourishtherapy.org', '1426 E 820 N, Orem, UT 84097', 'https://www.facebook.com/flourishtherapyinc/', null, true, null, null),
  ('PoD.2Pv7SOCsrclEza7j1g', 'Food & Friends Cache Valley', 'Social Groups', 'Cache County', array['Cache County']::text[], array['Gay Men']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f5634b6386cb4186df1b6ee_5f2e13894563bb3639285413_Food20Friends20Edited.jpeg', 'We are a gay men''s social group in the Cache Valley that meets monthly for dinner, conversation, board games, and/or movie nights. We meet on 2nd Saturday of every month at 6 PM either at a local restaurant (different restaurant each month) or at a member''s house for potluck dinner. Join us to try food from different restaurants in Cache Valley while making new friends or catching up with old ones.We welcome all gay/bi/trans men, 18 yrs and up. We don''t have to be residents of Cache Valley as we have friends from SLC that had attended our gatherings. We are a friendly, supportive and are nonjudgmental group of like-minded men who like trying different cuisines and have fun socializing. We ask that everyone be respectful as some of our members may not be "out".', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/loganfoodandfriends/', null, false, null, null),
  ('nusCmgC.TViJNbIBViQlUQ', 'For The Strength of LGBTQ & SSA Youth Online Community', 'Online Community', null, '{}'::text[], array['Youth']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f663c89dc4ac15aa61147df_novo-logo-afirma_o_n_(1).png', 'The Facebook page listed below is a portal for the For the Strength of LGBTQ/SSA Youth Facebook group which is "Secret." The group is specifically for straight and LGBTQ/SSA LDS youth ages 12-18 to support one another and is moderated by LDS youth with the supervision of a few straight/cis parents and two LDS therapists. If you are a youth age 12-18 and would like to join, leave a message with the page or email below.', null, null, 'fsymod@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/pages/For-the-Strength-of-LGBTQ-SSA-Youth/1454433078181817', null, false, null, null),
  ('IF-R53t2QQGmsJJdDu5uag', 'Fourth Street Clinic', 'Wellness/Medical', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/61148eb234645f19f9e35c8f_fourth.jpg', null, 'fourthstreetclinic.org', '801-364-0058', 'info@fourthstreetclinic.org', '409 West 400 South, Salt Lake City, Utah 84101', 'https://www.facebook.com/FourthStreetClinic/', 'https://www.instagram.com/4thstreetclinic/', true, null, null),
  ('VMbAOidgTdyaYXNUhVsc5Q', 'Full Circle Wellness Center', 'Social Groups', 'Cache County', array['Cache County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5fb544bc0c4524dde879ec03_74620919_150459412994725_5498206812085682176_o_(1).png', 'Full Circle Wellness Center host various monthly LGBTQ events at their center including yoga meetups, business cultural competency trainings, potlucks, etc. Full Circle Wellness Center is also an LGBTQ friendly business offering Ionic foot detox baths, reiki, foot zoning, light therapy, wellness related classes, meditation circles, nutritional therapy, message, tarot reading and health/wellness products.', null, '435-720-1096', 'fullcirclewellnesscenter.ut@gmail.com', '60 S Main St Suite 101, Brigham City, UT 84302', 'https://www.facebook.com/fullcirclewellnessutah/?ref=page_internal', null, false, null, null),
  ('hNoTLhsfRay9lR0usGZayw', 'Full Spectrum Coaching', 'Professional Services', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County','Utah County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/61781f7497015f3f2397a810_Copy_of_Unnamed_Design.png', null, null, '801-872-3394', 'trh.fullspectrumcoaching@gmail.com', null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/coach_tay1/', false, null, null),
  ('EzWOzMFwQ9CsQCcRifnN3Q', 'Gay Latter Day Saint Crossroads', 'Other', null, '{}'::text[], array['LDS']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/60b4fe32eacdd873063e6ff4_Gay_Latter-Day_Saint_Crossroads.png', 'Evan Smith believed the anti-gay messages he heard in church during his childhood, which contributed to some negative experiences on his mission in San Francisco. Later, as a bishop and then a counselor in a stake presidency,his heart softened as church members came to him seeking guidance about feeling attracted to others of the same gender. Evan’s investigating and study became personal when his own son came out as gay.In this navigable e-book, Evan tackles the issues with a lawyer’s mind and a penetrating analysis of scriptures and church doctrine. He addresses such questions as these: “What insights apply from the end of polygamy and the racebased priesthood/temple ban?” “Why do I stay in the church?” and, most importantly, “What words are hurtful/helpful to LGBTQ people and their families?”', 'https://www.gayldscrossroads.org/', null, 'contact@gayldscrossroads.org', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/GayLDSCrossroads/', null, true, null, null),
  ('Rr5NUCyeT7KNHsQFr67Xbw', 'GB: Parents of Trans Kids (On Hiatus)', 'Support Circles', 'Utah County', array['Utah County']::text[], array['Parent','Trans']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f2b30c0782f831652b5c0a7_Genderbands.png', 'Hey there, friends. Genderbands has an announcement. 

We are taking a temporary hiatus from most of our services so we can come back stronger and better equipped to meet the needs of our beloved transgender community. We know this may feel disappointing to some of you, but we are committed to our mission of helping transgender people pay for transition-related costs, and pausing to regroup is a necessary step in continuing our work. Here are a few things you can expect during our hiatus:
 
Grant applications will open in the Fall of 2023, and the next grant recipients will be announced in 2024.
Our retail store will continue to operate on a limited basis.
We are no longer accepting new applications for our free binder program, but we will do our best to honor all applications we have already received. 
Email response time will be slower than typical during the hiatus.
You will still fin', 'genderbands.org/hiatus', null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
