Our retail store will continue to operate on a limited basis.
We are no longer accepting new applications for our free binder program, but we will do our best to honor all applications we have already received. 
Email response time will be slower than typical during the hiatus.
You will still fin', 'genderbands.org/hiatus', null, null, '51 West Center St #341 Orem, UT 84057, USA', 'https://www.facebook.com/genderbands/', 'https://www.instagram.com/genderbands/', false, null, null),
  ('7l6IJOCVQ36p0vTUqign-w', 'Give Back Utah', 'Homeless', 'Utah County', array['Utah County','Salt Lake County']::text[], array['Adults']::text[], 'https://storage.googleapis.com/glide-prod.appspot.com/uploads-v2/vZEd46xUe6vz0E68sGvW/pub/KfklHmeIDHSnwgQWgqoS.jpeg', 'We are a local volunteer service looking to have others join our team to lend a hand to those in need. Our hope is to assist these people who want to become self sufficient and take back control of their lives.', 'givebackutah.org', null, 'info@givebackutah.org', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100068836710139', null, true, null, null),
  ('fFjyRknJQeWruTArbh7m0w', 'GLSEN Northern Utah', 'Education/Advocacy', null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/61148f6c505200cfe17c02e1_default-share-img--facebook.jpg', 'GLSEN Northern Utah is a chapter of GLSEN, a national organization fighting for every student’s right to a safe, supportive education. 

GLSEN Northern Utah is a grassroots initiative, working locally in our community to ensure safe schools for all students, regardless of sexual orientation and gender identity. There are 43 Chapters around the country doing this important work. Join us today!
Our chapter supports students and educators locally, organizes around LGBTQ-affirming public policy, plans teacher trainings, and hosts events for students, educators, parents, and allies. Chapters like ours play an important role in bringing GLSEN’s programs and visions to right where we live, work, and learn. While some chapters have full-time or part-time staff, most are entirely volunteer-based. We''re always looking for new volunteers to help us ensure safe schools for all students.', 'https://www.glsen.org/chapter/northern-utah', null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/GLSEN', 'https://www.instagram.com/glsen/', false, null, null),
  ('t95Nf0c-StWlc7-TDxI-mw', 'Health Insurance Provider Search', 'Wellness/Medical', null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/61148fb34b7aa72bda794aeb_2017-01-13-health-insurance.jpg', 'Use the following links below to find in-network providers within your health insurance plan.', null, null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('V4bYF3FVTr-F5DKdqFGrrg', 'Help Me Flourish: Parent and Caregiver Support Group', 'Support Circles', 'Utah County', array['Utah County','Davis County','Salt Lake County']::text[], array['Parent']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5fa5e1cd79f25bc54ed2dd82_cropped-Copy-of-Flourish-Icon.png', 'Christine Hubbard, Social Work Associate at Flourish Therapy, hosts an educational support group for parents and caregivers of LGBTQIA youth. 6 Topics. 1.5 hours a week to talk and learn. Need support and knowledge? Register below!

 Topics include: 

1- Basics of Gender and Sexual Identity

2- Body Image and Development of Self Esteem

3- How to Talk to Your LGBTQIA Kids About Sex

4- Helping Your Kids Build a Support Network 

5- Coping As Parents', 'https://forms.gle/PMF12zzE2d8Hok9c6', null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('XG6AVndmTUO8j0iKydsJ7g', 'Human Rights Campaign', 'Education/Advocacy', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5fa5e290c79d7b80376e57fa_unnamed.jpg', 'Our Mission: By inspiring and engaging individuals and communities, the Human Rights Campaign strives to end discrimination against LGBTQ people and realize a world that achieves fundamental fairness and equality for all. HRC envisions a world where lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender and queer people are ensured equality and embraced as full members of society at home, at work and in every community.', 'utah.hrc.org', '202-628-4160', 'hrcutahvolunteers@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/hrc.utah/', 'https://www.instagram.com/hrcutah/', true, null, null),
  ('OKfOHoTfSiGAlgDpMZKfCg', 'I''ll Walk With You', 'Video Project', null, '{}'::text[], array['LDS']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5f5637d9d20ccc0db6248ac1_5f2c881346237b6a67ee1976_I%2527ll%2520Walk%2520With%2520You.jpeg', 'These videos were created for Latter-day Saint parents and allies to voice their love for their LGBT brothers and sisters, sons and daughters. They want to give a message of comfort and support to other parents who are navigating the difficult conflicts that can arise in families around this issue. Each video offers a unique perspective, but all of the participants are united in a concern for individuals and families who might be struggling and even suffering because of misunderstandings. The participants are also united in the belief that their LDS religion offers them the tools to resolve these problems in a way that allows for health and growth of each member of the family and preserves the unity and strength of family bonds. Most of these families are also willing to communicate with parents and individuals who are looking for advice and support. If you are new to this issue or if yo', 'ldswalkwithyou.org', null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('O4ddJ23.TSayjrxRmY6xWA', 'It Gets Better', 'Video Project', null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5f5637d8c04fcd0094f27b14_5f2d99dcfeb406f686539c20_USGA.jpeg', 'In 2012, gay BYU students from the Understanding Same-Gender Attraction (USGA) group created the “It Gets Better” video series in order to promote conversation and understanding for those with same-sex attraction on campus. Kendall Wilcox, a former employee at BYUtv and (at the time) member of the USGA stated “The primary intent [of the video] was to just send a message of love, hope and community to LGBT Mormon youth who are at their most vulnerable, who may be questioning their self-worth and their status before God. . . We want this video to send the message that there is hope, they have a future, there is hope for love and happiness in the future.”', 'usgabyu.com/it-gets-better', null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('2QmWtOiDTaKH5.EN6P6aAA', 'Journeys of Faith', 'Blog', null, '{}'::text[], array['LDS']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5fb495d33c18f3515b791d62_north%20star.jpg', 'The Journeys of Faith Project features the personal stories of Latter-day Saint individuals and families addressing gender identity or transgenderism who are striving to find congruence and peace within the context of faith in the gospel of Jesus Christ.

Their stories allow each of us a glimpse into their inner experience, inviting us into a place of greater awareness and empathy for an aspect of the human experience so personal and poignant to some of our brothers and sisters. As they struggle to address a difficult and complex issue with few answers, and as we walk with them on their personal journeys, they remind us what it means to live by faith.', 'https://t2m.io/journeys-of-faith', null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('VVjJg745R6CCN1.wpEdckQ', 'Journeys Online Community', 'Online Community', null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f663c89dc4ac15aa61147df_novo-logo-afirma_o_n.png', 'Affirmation Journeys is a group oriented toward LGBTQIA, their families, and allies who are transitioning out of Mormon orthodoxy, as well as former Mormons. We welcome everybody, but the discussions will be from a perspective of those who are either Mormons undergoing a faith transition, unorthodox Mormons, non-believing Mormons or former Mormons. The group will be open to all topics of particular interest to this community, but it will have a particular goal of helping people move forward in healthy productive ways as they proceed during or following a faith transition.', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/572382942892407/', null, false, null, null),
  ('6uBFwWk3T7qAy0-5pteinQ', 'Lesbian Adults Friendship Circle', 'Support Circles', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County','Utah County','Washington County']::text[], array['Lesbian']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/Encircle_Logo.png', 'This friendship circle is for adults (18+) who identify as lesbian. 

Friendship Circles?
These groups are designed to provide connection with folx you identify with and help you manage the trials you encounter every day. Friendship Circles create an opportunity for you to take control and thrive in your own life.

Friendship Circles provide opportunities for sharing, connection, and support through discussion of issues and experiences relevant to each group, often exploring the intersectionality of conservative cultures, spirituality, sexuality, social issues, transitional issues, and health issues and the ways it impacts us. The groups also provide a great support network—members in similar circumstances with similar feelings with whom they can share in an open and unedited fashion.

Groups organized by sexuality, age, and/or gender identity.

For schedules and more information please ', null, null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('JP7DRTkJSGiqIYer096OkA', 'LGBT Mormon People of Color and Allies Online Community', 'Online Community', null, '{}'::text[], array['QPOC']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f663c89dc4ac15aa61147df_novo-logo-afirma_o_n.png', 'The Affirmation: LGBT Mormons, Families, and Friends People of Color and Allies Group is a group of self-identified people of color and allies gathered to explore multiple identities and the intersections of race/ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, and LDS faith.', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/134166980037744/', null, false, null, null),
  ('c81ITvxyT5-mmeS32NNT4w', 'LGBTQ & Allied Lawyers of Utah', 'Professional Services', null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5f5633381f80e62355331c42_5f36a85aa8337617b7ec894a_LGBTQ%2520Allied%2520Lawyers%2520of%2520Utah.png', 'LGBT & Allied Lawyers of Utah is a group of lawyers serving lawyers. We are an association of the Utah State Bar and an affiliate of the National LGBT Bar Association. Our mission is to use education and advocacy to promote and support the rights of LGBT people within the legal profession and throughout Utah.We are sometimes contacted by people who are seeking legal advice or looking to hire an attorney who specializes in LGBTQ issues. We have created this directory to assist these potential clients. The attorneys listed below represent clients on LGBTQ issues. While we believe this is an excellent list, we have not verified any of the information they provided. We list every attorney who requests to be added.', 'https://t2m.io/lgbt-and-allied-lawyers-of-utah', null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('rMsGLPWHQUi2OJEvDGLSIQ', 'LGBTQ Adult Friendship Circle', 'Support Circles', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County','Utah County','Washington County']::text[], array['LGBTQ Adults']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/Encircle_Logo.png', 'This friendship circle is for adults (25+) that identify as LGBTQ+.

