Groups organized by sexuality, age, and/or gender identity.

For schedules and more information please ', null, null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('m2kG6ztITCafO6zAT5qX-A', 'LGBTQ Affirmative Therapist Guild of Utah', 'Mental Health/Counseling', null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5fbd5b121c01c36c2e81264c_Therapists%20guild.png', 'The LGBTQ-Affirmative Psychotherapist Guild of Utah is a Utah-based, grassroots organization of licensed mental-health professionals and students-in-training. We share a collaborative commitment to make affirmative culturally competent therapy available for anyone.The Guild believes that all individuals and families deserve mental health services that affirm sexual and gender diversity. To this end, we provide innovative and affirmative training to mental health professionals and trainees grounded in values of cultural humility, social advocacy, collaboration, and inclusivity. We believe this work honors and celebrates the lived experiences of sexual and gender diverse individuals, families, and communities while promoting justice and dignity.LGBTQ Affirming Therapist DirectoryA directory of self-reported LGBTQ Affirmative therapists in Utah. <a href="http://www.lgbtqtherapists.com/direc', 'https://t2m.io/lgbtq-therapists-guild', '(385) 355-0965', 'robin@lgbtqtherapists.com', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/LGBTQATGU/', null, true, null, null),
  ('5T.ks.E7Rfq7ZW.4gS5bBQ', 'LGBTQ and Allies in Wards, Stakes and Missions', 'Online Community', null, '{}'::text[], array['LDS']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/612ad970e84a8fdb08668d72_Untitled%20design%20(6).png', 'This is a group of active Latter-day Saints (LGBTQ, Allies and Local Leaders) who are working in Ward, Stake, Seminaries and Institutes, Church Schools, or Mission Leadership to put together LGBTQ meetings, firesides, FHEs, materials, class discussions, Church talks, etc.

The purpose is to share ideas, materials, approaches, events so that each person does not feel they are starting from scratch or alone in their efforts.
President Ballard asked us to council together—and this virtual group gives us a chance to do that—and come up with the right plan/approach for your area of influence.
It is not a place to debate Church doctrine or policy.

Posts not focused on this topic will be removed (sorry my friends, but really want to keep the focus on the mission statement).
You are welcome to invite others to the group. Remind them to answer the two questions that are required to join the grou', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/1433556613672143', null, false, null, null),
  ('hfF.2JO2Sv2zJDCh-AJFTw', 'LGBTQ Youth Friendship Circle', 'Support Circles', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County','Utah County','Washington County']::text[], array['Youth']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/Encircle_Logo.png', 'This friendship circle is for LGBTQ+ youth between the ages of 12-17.

Friendship Circles?
These groups are designed to provide connection with folx you identify with and help you manage the trials you encounter every day. Friendship Circles create an opportunity for you to take control and thrive in your own life.

Friendship Circles provide opportunities for sharing, connection, and support through discussion of issues and experiences relevant to each group, often exploring the intersectionality of conservative cultures, spirituality, sexuality, social issues, transitional issues, and health issues and the ways it impacts us. The groups also provide a great support network—members in similar circumstances with similar feelings with whom they can share in an open and unedited fashion.

Groups organized by sexuality, age, and/or gender identity.

For schedules and more information please', null, null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('9ag3Ln6RSQ6ssduiLol-MQ', 'LGBTQ+ Workplace Education Center', 'Education/Advocacy', 'Washington County', array['Washington County']::text[], array['Allies']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/60b40d3855e085624f5b4c33_44395299_349313352496545_6980696748045893632_n.png', 'We help you create inclusive spaces where LGBTQ employees can thrive. LGBTQ+ cultural competency training on demand through e-learning courses. Diversity and inclusion training for your entire team has never been easier!', 'lgbtqworkplace.com', null, 'info@lgbtqworkplace.com', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/lgbtq.education.center/', 'https://www.instagram.com/lgbtq_workplace/', true, null, null),
  ('Mmh-q5EiRCech3hOFq91Qg', 'LGBTQIA+ and Allies in Medicine at UUSOM', 'College Resources', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/61149051fa744a3212772e2c_BlockU_400px.png', 'To increase awareness and education concerning LGBTQIA+ healthcare issues as well as provide a social and support network for University of Utah medical students, health sciences students, residents, and faculty who identify as LGBTQIA+.
Need a safe space? Head to the "Synapse" in the basement of the Health Sciences Library. This space is designed for students to have a place to go where they can feel comfortable, relax, or study. There are couches, coffee makers, and plenty of study spaces available!', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/154740254907507/', 'https://instagram.com/utahallies?igshid=9s4bg39c7s1j', false, null, null),
  ('XaaLGelPSlSTQKv9a9AqHQ', 'Lift + Love', 'Resource Page', null, '{}'::text[], array['LDS','Parent']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/60f882f0c3c4dd0ba35e5561_Lift%2BLove.PNG', 'My husband, Kenn, and I live in Salt Lake and have three amazing children and a brand-new son-in-law We are a regular LDS LGBTQ family.

As the mother of an LGBTQ child and a member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints, I have learned to rely on the Lord and trust the Inspiration I received. My goal is to keep all of my children connected to their Savior and to teach them to face life with courage and confidence

I learned this growing up in my own LGBTQ family. My oldest brother, Preston was gay. Raising a gay child in the 70s and 80s my parents were on their own to navigate what it meant to be an openly gay family in the church. It was not easy and neither they nor my brother felt supported. But they did the best they could

In 2017, my brother took his own life. At the same time, my oldest son was starting his own process of coming out. My brother''s painful life was a to', 'liftandlove.org', null, null, null, null, 'http://instagram.com/liftandloveorg', false, null, null),
  ('c8gx2LgFQ0iokHpvKfYbNg', 'Lift + Love LGBTQ+ Mamas (Parents) Community', 'Support Circles', null, '{}'::text[], array['Parent']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/60f882f0c3c4dd0ba35e5561_Lift%2BLove.PNG', 'We are excited to have you join this growing group of LDS mothers who want to raise healthy LGBTQ children.  There is wisdom in this community of faithful women and strength in knowing that you are not alone.', 'liftandlove.org/#/meeting/', null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('NBTusl96R.iaVi.yfvTOlw', 'Living Waters Online Community', 'Online Community', null, '{}'::text[], array['LDS']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f663c89dc4ac15aa61147df_novo-logo-afirma_o_n.png', 'Affirmation Journeys is a group oriented toward LGBTQIA, their families, and allies who are transitioning out of Mormon orthodoxy, as well as former Mormons. We welcome everybody, but the discussions will be from a perspective of those who are either Mormons undergoing a faith transition, unorthodox Mormons, non-believing Mormons or former Mormons. The group will be open to all topics of particular interest to this community, but it will have a particular goal of helping people move forward in healthy productive ways as they proceed during or following a faith transition.', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/taliatha.holmes', null, false, null, null),
