  ('OZ8barp0S4WiljLciOrg.w', 'Stockton Powers Memorial Scholarship', 'College Resources', null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5f5630a01dc0c314cac46b3f_5f36b24f6baf8e9e7fa053d0_Stockton%2520Powers%2520Memorial%2520Scholarship.png', 'GENERAL INFO

The Stockton Powers Memorial Scholarship is available to those who apply for themselves or for those who believe there is someone who is deserving of this scholarship. The scholarship may be applied to tuition cost, book fees, housing, educational tools, and daily expenses. Recipient will receive a certain dollar amount according to needs*. Please contact us with any questions about eligibility or if you need any help applying.

ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA

In order to be eligible to apply for the Stockton Powers Memorial Scholarship, you must meet the following requirements:

High School Senior to 25 years of age

Furthering your education

Utah applicants only

Maintain a GPA of 2.8 or above 

WHY WE DO ITStockton was born in Salt Lake City, UT on May 5, 1999. He was a long-awaited blessing for our family. Stockton was very adventurous. Whatever he loved, he gave 110%. He loved ', 'https://www.standingforstockton.com/', null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('KPCWMwu-Sa-Y4S5vFCRMuw', 'Stonewall Sports', 'Social Groups', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5fbd74565cd65ce2d7a50639_download%20(13).png', 'WHO WE ARE: 

Stonewall Sports - Salt Lake City is an LGBTQ+ and Ally not-for-profit sports league. We strive to develop a well-connected and diverse community through organized competition and social or fundraising events.

 
VISION: Our Vision is that EVERY person should have the ability to feel comfortable playing organized sports and that we have the responsibility to give back to our community. 

MISSION: Our Mission is to provide an inclusive, low cost, high FUN sports league that is managed as a non-profit with a philanthropic heart. 

Stonewall Sports Salt Lake City was founded in 2018 to create an inclusive community that has fun through playing sports and giving back with a philanthropic heart. We are an LGBTQ+ organization that celebrates allies and people from all walks of life. Please find a sport that you love and join! We hope you can meet some new friends and have a blast', 'http://www.stonewallsportsslc.org/', null, 'saltlakecity@stonewallsports.org', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/SLCSTONEWALL/', 'https://www.instagram.com/stonewallsportsslc/', true, null, null),
  ('G8tGnuBNQcueevw8wJ14QA', 'SUU Pride Alliance Sexuality and Gender Resources', 'College Resources', 'Washington County', array['Washington County']::text[], array['LGBTQ+ Adult','Student']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5f5642cf508736f345ad976b_SUU%20Pride%20Alliance.png', 'The Center for Diversity and Inclusion is committed to advocating for our lesbian, gay, bisexual, trans, queer, intersex, and asexual (LGBTQIA+) students, staff, and community members. We believe in creating an environment where sexual and gender diversity is respected and celebrated. As a Center, we resist any actions contrary to the health and success of our LGBTQIA+ communities.', 'https://www.suu.edu/pridealliance/resources.html', '435-865-8482', 'pridealliance@suu.edu', '351 W University Blvd. Cedar City, Utah 84720', 'https://www.facebook.com/SUUPAEC/', 'https://www.instagram.com/suu_paec/', true, null, null),
  ('kSY-1gQjTMupHhFLNujwkg', 'TEA of Utah', 'Education/Advocacy', null, '{}'::text[], array['Trans']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5fb96b6ee5e1d88b0072fdc3_TEA.jpg', 'To our LGBTQIA+ students, please know you belong here. You are supported, you are valid, and you are not alone. We look forward to working alongside you.', 'https://www.teaofutah.org/', null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/TEAofUtah.org/', null, false, null, null),
  ('75jAyg.OQ-GsEl7O1p2N.w', 'Teen Support Group', 'Support Circles', 'Cache County', array['Cache County']::text[], array['Young Adult']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5f358fc72b040487de0d14ba_Cache%20Pride.jpg', 'Cache Pride Center gives youth a physical and emotionally safe space. Each week we provide a hot meal and check-in with our youth. Our groups are tailored to the needs of our youths through support groups, one-on-one therapy, individually crafted lessons to develop lifelong skills, creative expression workshops, games, peer support, guided discussions, sexuality education, and during the school year, an hour of tutoring to see our youth succeed in school. During our groups, our youth have access to food, clothing, and hygiene items to provide for their basic needs. We also provide assistance in accessing affirming health care, mental health care, local organizations, suicide prevention and additional relevant resources.Teen (Ages 14-18)596 E 900 N, Logan, UT 84321Fridays 5pm – 8pmFor LGBTQIAP+ youth', 'cachepridecenter.org', '(435) 363-5473', 'cachepridecenter@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/CachePrideCenter/', null, true, null, null),
  ('jHIDim61T3CcvZ4xHRgIzQ', 'The OUT Foundation', 'College Resources', 'Utah County', array['Utah County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/6125a653c64d94f83d551580_Bee_logo_Artboard%201.png', 'Our mission is to empower the LGBTQ+ students and alumni of Brigham Young University in achieving their intellectual, social, and professional potential. We do this by completing initiatives based on the needs of our students and alumni.', 'https://www.theout.foundation/', '(801) 691-6149', 'info@theout.foundation', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/theOUTfoundation/', 'https://instagram.com/theoutfoundation?igshid=1q6cgtiz1prc8', true, null, null),
  ('FGJaqfbKT6Sm9h3zw5VhHA', 'The Royal Court of the Golden Spike Empire', 'Philanthropy', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/6114929acf584a497d4e49af_GSA.jpg', 'The Royal Court is a registered 501 c(3) organization and is, in fact, Utah’s oldest LGBTQ+ Organization. Founded in 1976, we were originally established as a social organization for the LGBTQ+ community of Utah to have a safe place to gather and raise money for various groups and organizations in Utah.  We have been a part of many firsts in the Salt Lake City LGBTQ+ community and even started the yearly pride celebration that is so popular today.  Many members of our Founders Table are still around and still a part of the many great things that we do.

As the years progressed, and the issues facing the community changed, our focus changed to helping individuals in need. We began focusing on people dealing with Cancer, HIV / Aids, the Youth, and Transgender individuals, just to name a few. We have many funds that our community members may apply to for financial assistance.  We have our P', 'rcgse.org', null, 'info@rcgse.org', 'https://www.facebook.com/rcgse', null, null, true, null, null),
  ('AZ5c1MHcR4iQzmjVTsPmDA', 'The Utah Hearth', 'Speaker Series', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], array['LDS']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/603bd6ae966471da0bdba72f_THE%20HEARTH%20(2).png', 'An inclusive community of LGBTQ Latter-Day Saints and those who love them. The Utah Hearth is an organization that invites monthly speakers to share their stories and messages in an effort to support, encourage, and offer hope to LGBTQ Latter-Day Saint members and those that love them. Attendants usually comprise of LGBTQ individuals and family members that are current, or former, members of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints. Events are usually held the first Sunday of every month in Holladay. Past speakers have included Barbara and Steve Young (NFL/Love Loud Foundation), George and Alyson Deussen (Stockton Powers Memorial Scholarship/Peculiar), and Richard Ostler (Listen Learn and Love Podcast).', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/320445228673183', null, false, null, null),
  ('YrPjRAG2QACU6YiBdeZ2Dg', 'Trans* Mormons, Families, & Friends Online Community', 'Online Community', null, '{}'::text[], array['Trans','LDS']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/5f663c89dc4ac15aa61147df_novo-logo-afirma_o_n.png', 'Affirmation Trans* is an inclusive group for Trans* Mormons, and their friends and family. We encourage learning and education of Trans* topics and how they relate to both daily life and the restored gospel. Our goal is to create a welcoming community for Trans* brothers and sisters in Affirmation, where we can find a safe space to learn, grow, and teach through uplifting discussion and heartfelt stories.', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/674629102608451/', null, false, null, null),
  ('0H6ayeU1TMqFP1FddjAIeg', 'TransAction', 'Support Circles', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], array['Trans']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/60b3f1a3f51b70dd9c04c702_11080978_353214928198566_330726561824751880_n.jpg', 'The mission of TransAction is to create social community, offer mentorship, and teach life skills to the trans and gender non-binary communities.', null, '801-539-8800', 'transaction@utahpridecenter.org', '1380 S. Main Street, Salt Lake City', 'https://www.facebook.com/transactionut/', null, false, null, null),
  ('yAOVjMjTSe2fBpQ96Map2w', 'Transactive LDS Support Group', 'Online Community', null, '{}'::text[], array['Trans','LDS']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/60b3f1a3f51b70dd9c04c702_11080978_353214928198566_330726561824751880_n.jpg', 'A faith affirming group to help Transgender/Intersex/Gender Dysphoria individuals and their family members support one another. Group members may be active or former LDS to join, as long as a tone of respect for LDS beliefs is maintained.', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/TransActiveLDS/?ref=page_internal', null, false, null, null),
  ('CFn4NwTLS0GyLVCbYChwtw', 'Transgender Adults Friendship Circle', 'Support Circles', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County','Washington County','Utah County']::text[], array['Trans']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/Encircle_Logo.png', 'This friendship circle is for transgender folx over the age of 18. 

Friendship Circles?
These groups are designed to provide connection with folx you identify with and help you manage the trials you encounter every day. Friendship Circles create an opportunity for you to take control and thrive in your own life.

Friendship Circles provide opportunities for sharing, connection, and support through discussion of issues and experiences relevant to each group, often exploring the intersectionality of conservative cultures, spirituality, sexuality, social issues, transitional issues, and health issues and the ways it impacts us. The groups also provide a great support network—members in similar circumstances with similar feelings with whom they can share in an open and unedited fashion.

Groups organized by sexuality, age, and/or gender identity.

For schedules and more information please v', null, null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('dYx8AdLsQ9SecbSdnEJREQ', 'Trevor Space', 'Online Community', null, '{}'::text[], array['LGBTQ']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/611492cfa68fb607cc85bda6_the-trevor-project-donation-o.jpg', 'Start meeting LGBTQ friends today!

TrevorSpace is an affirming international community for LGBTQ young people ages 13-24. Sign up and start a conversation now.', 'https://www.trevorspace.org/?utm_source=trevor_website&utm_medium=web&utm_campaign=nav_bar', null, null, null, null, null, false, null, null),
  ('9c.fhO7DSfGwy0stlvMpxQ', 'University of Utah LGBT Resource Center', 'College Resources', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/61149051fa744a3212772e2c_BlockU_400px.png', 'The LGBT Resource Center empowers lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender, queer, questioning, intersex, asexual/aromatic (LGBTQIA+) students to grow as leaders and learners by supporting students in navigating university systems, exploring their identities, finding community, and developing as leaders with a social justice lens.', 'https://lgbt.utah.edu/', '801-587-7973', 'lgbtrc@sa.utah.edu', '200 S. CENTRAL CAMPUS DR, SALT LAKE CITY, UT 84112', 'https://www.facebook.com/LGBTResource/', 'https://www.instagram.com/lgbtresource/?hl=en', true, null, null),
  ('j8Q1Rs8gT1SHABwWxtgryg', 'University of Utah Transgender Health Program', 'Wellness/Medical', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], array['Trans']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/61149051fa744a3212772e2c_BlockU_400px.png', 'The Transgender Health Program at the University of Utah Health brings quality healthcare to trans adults and teens from all walks of life. We welcome all identities and expressions seeking our services. We understand that every trans or gender-nonconforming person’s experience is unique. Our doctors will be there to give you endless support wherever your journey takes you.

Your comfort and trust matter the most to us. We provide a safe, trans-affirmative environment where patients can comfortably access the full range of health services they need. This includes primary care; surgery and hormone therapy; and mental health, counseling, and nutrition services. We will even help you navigate your care and finances to find the best care that fits your budget.', 'healthcare.utah.edu/transgender-health', '801-213-2195', 'transgenderhealth@hsc.utah.edu', null, null, null, true, null, null),
  ('9BkpJzZER7-7o7S5V1jfKQ', 'Utah AIDS Foundation', 'Wellness/Medical', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5fb286359815020668a1db2a_UAF.jpeg', 'MISSION

Utah AIDS Foundation, through client-driven services, champions sexual health and overall well-being for those living with or at risk for HIV and other STIs.

VISION 

Utah AIDS Foundation works to achieve a future where everyone has equitable access to HIV and STI education, prevention, treatment, and care. 

SERVICES

The Utah AIDS Foundation provides support to people living with HIV/AIDS, and prevention services for those at risk for HIV.    We offer assistance and expertise to anyone struggling with the complex issues that surround HIV, because we believe that no one should have to confront this disease alone.

 - HIV/STI Testing

- HIV/STI Info Hotline

- Case Management & Support

- Food Bank

- Educational Presentations

- Syringe Exchange', 'utahaids.org', '801-487-2323', null, '1408 1100 E, Salt Lake City, UT 84105', 'https://www.facebook.com/utahaidsfoundation', 'https://www.instagram.com/utahaidsfoundation/', true, null, null),
  ('60OfnduNReWDinYhDh7XOw', 'Utah Asexuals', 'Social Groups', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], array['Asexual']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5fb2d7100e504cfd3b8145c5_download.png', 'Utah Asexuals strives to develop a welcoming and open environment that stands for inclusion, affirmation, and support for all the asexual &amp; aromantic community of Utah.', null, null, 'utahasexuals@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/UTAces', null, false, null, null),
  ('DBmBhJTGQKiH9x16w3FIUA', 'Utah Bears', 'Social Groups', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], array['Gay Men']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/6114931ba68fb60b9085bdd4_idRc1AK6.jpg', 'We are a men’s membership-based social and service group organized and operated exclusively to support and to promote diversity and inclusion in our community; foster positive community involvement; and provide opportunities which enhance the personal growth of our members, the Bear community, and the LGBT community as a whole.', 'utahbears.com', null, 'info@utahbears.com', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/utahbears/', 'https://www.instagram.com/utahbearsinc/', true, null, null),
  ('46Lawh8hTj6.cmMUJZTMlw', 'Utah Center for Legal Inclusion', 'Professional Services', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], array['Adults']::text[], 'https://storage.googleapis.com/glide-prod.appspot.com/uploads-v2/vZEd46xUe6vz0E68sGvW/pub/OvuFnk21v0chv4YquLTy.png', 'The Utah Center for Legal Inclusion (UCLI) is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization dedicated to advancing the goals of equity and inclusion in Utah’s legal profession. By coordinating with the Utah State Bar and its affinity groups, legal employers, government agencies, educational institutions, and community partners, UCLI strives to enhance organizational inclusion, facilitate educational opportunities and professional advancement for students and attorneys with diverse backgrounds, assist in eliminating bias in Utah’s justice system, and track the progress of legal inclusion efforts throughout the state. UCLI invites all to participate in its inclusion initiatives, which will help strengthen Utah’s legal institutions in an increasingly diverse state.', 'https://www.utahcli.org', '(801) 746 – 5221', 'ucli@utahcli.org', '645 South 200 East
Salt Lake City, Utah 84111', 'https://www.facebook.com/UtahUCLI/', 'https://www.instagram.com/utahcli', true, null, null),
  ('WhEuMxUmSmSTmApqMSHAnw', 'Utah Coalition Against Sexual Assault - LGBTQ Coordinating Counsel', 'Education/Advocacy', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/61149346f9a74f1e9aeb944c_logo-comb.png', 'Our Statewide LGBTQ Coordinating Council Advisory Council (Council) is a permanent advisory council located within the Utah Coalition Against Sexual Assault (UCASA). It was established by a vote of the Board of Directors in 2017 to ensure that LGBTQ survivors and victims of sexual violence are represented in victim services organizations, institutions, and partnerships that serve sexual violence survivors statewide. This includes but is not limited to:

Ensuring adequate representation of LGBTQ survivors in all Sexual Assault Response Teams (SARTs) statewide.

Ensuring that LGBTQ-affirming training is provided statewide to sexual violence programs, law enforcement, and any other institution that interacts with sexual violence survivors.

Ensuring that print, online, and others forms of information are available online to improve services for LGBTQ survivors of sexual violence.

Producing', 'https://www.ucasa.org/lgbtqq', '801-746-0404', 'info@ucasa.org', '284 West 400 North Salt Lake City, Utah 84103', null, null, true, null, null),
  ('ldTmxD4IRViHvtbh8.PiWw', 'Utah FAM', 'Education/Advocacy', null, '{}'::text[], array['LGBTQ']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/60b3a872bb547ffdf40cf9e3_Untitled%20design%20(8).png', 'Founded Kody Colvin, Alli Martin, and Tyson Price in 2016, Utah FAM works to make Utah schools better for LGBTQ+ teachers and students. Utah FAM has delivered hundreds of professional learning workshops, seminars, and trainings at schools, companies, and homes. We organize monthly educator socials via Zoom open to teachers across the state. We make new friends, celebrate successes, share ideas and resources, and provide individualized support.

Utah FAM educators seek to empower LGBTQ+ teachers and allies to embed LGBTQ+ affirming practice into schools and classrooms.', 'https://utahfam.org/', null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/FAM.SLC', 'https://www.instagram.com/fam_utah/', false, null, null),
  ('FXwte0KgT4KRB32LiU7LsQ', 'Utah Fertility Clinic', 'Wellness/Medical', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County','Weber County','Washington County','Utah County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/61149380a2c309164b4cf77e_unnamed%20(1).jpg', 'LGBTQ Family Building

Everyone’s journey to parenthood is unique, and we strive to make this experience as seamless and comfortable as possible.  Whether you need donor sperm, donor eggs, or a gestational carrier (surrogate), our reproductive specialists and staff will help you to navigate the process to best fit your needs.  LGBTQ family building may involve intrauterine inseminations or In Vitro Fertilization, and we welcome the opportunity to help all couples or individuals conceive.

Fertility Treatment for Lesbian Couples


Treatment for lesbian couples is typically intrauterine inseminations (IUI) or In Vitro Fertilization (IVF) using donor sperm.  A consultation with one of our physicians and review of both partners’ medical history can help determine the most optimal treatment options. Questions to consider are whose eggs will be used and who will carry the baby.

Treatment for ', 'utahfertility.com', '801-785-5100', null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/UtahFertility', 'https://www.instagram.com/utahfertilitycenter/', true, null, null),
  ('MqC4lt.-QU2xEH2aYQPyhw', 'Utah Gay Fathers Association', 'Support Circles', null, '{}'::text[], array['Gay Men']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/611493b6f1c289074e6c8750_430720_255500641198412_2020205657_n.jpg', 'UGFA exists to provide support, community, and educational resources to Utah’s gay fathers and future fathers.

The Utah Gay Fathers Association is a group dedicated to holding monthly, in-person social gatherings of gay dads. Our focus is to embrace, affirm, and improve ourselves as gay fathers and men; to socialize and share the unique and universal joys, strengths, and challenges that we face as gay fathers in Utah. 

As a group we have discussions about what it means to be a gay father, current issues group members may be facing, helpful suggestions, venting, personal therapeutic or legal recommendations, etc.', null, null, 'utahgayfathers@gmail.com', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/utahgayfathers/', null, false, null, null),
  ('rOrhlNG0QiyDcdrErb2zRQ', 'Utah LGBT Young Adult Hangouts', 'Social Groups', 'Davis County', array['Davis County']::text[], array['Young Adult']::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/60a7d80564267c639e4bb108_Screenshot_20210212-160905-636.png', 'This is a safe place for LGBT+ teens and young adults to hangout, make friends, and connect with others. Events and Hangouts are held at the beginning of every month, hosted by Jessie Funk and Robby Talbot. Straight Allys wanted and welcome! Everyone is welcome, accepted, and loved. Come join! ♥️', null, null, null, null, 'https://www.facebook.com/groups/574420233039108', 'https://instagram.com/utahlgbthangouts?utm_medium=copy_link', false, null, null),
  ('4S-d-PPYQdCPPeM5aKN0uA', 'Utah LGBTQ+ Chamber of Commerce', 'Professional Services', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/611493d1cd52a7edb255b725_event-featured-Mic-1553122300.png', 'The Utah LGBTQ+ Chamber of Commerce is open to corporations of all sizes, sole proprietors and independent agents regardless of sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression. This is a great place to meet other professionals, make business contacts, promote your business and work for the enhancement of Utah’s LGBTQ+ community', 'https://www.utahlgbtqchamber.org/', '385-743-9211', 'boardofdirectors@utahlgbtqchamber.org', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/utahgaychamber/', 'https://www.instagram.com/utah.gay.chamber/', true, null, null),
