  ('3GXR-pxGT2OgBGoINLSnuA', 'WSU Matthew Shepherd Scholarship', 'College Resources', null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/6114942efa35a781b4d2f0df_athletics_stacked.jpg', 'The purpose of this endowed scholarship is to support students at Weber State University who identify as a sexual or gender minority as well as their allies. It is a goal of this scholarship to educate individuals about issues concerning sexual and gender minorities and to create an atmosphere of support and nurturing for all students at Weber State University. 

Scholarship applications are taken during Spring Semester and scholarships are awarded for the academic year starting in Fall Semester. Scholarship Awards can cover resident tuition, books, fees and other educational expenses. 

The Weber State University Matthew Shepard Scholarship strives to: 

Build awareness of the academic achievements and community service of sexual and gender minority students at Weber State University. 

 Encourage recipients to complete their studies and become an engaged, supportive community leader.

', 'weber.edu/lgbtresourcecenter/Matthew_Shepard_Scholarship.html', '801-626-7271', 'jaysonstokes@weber.edu', null, null, null, true, null, null),
  ('RYBSszqCT3GDOANhjCmJNg', 'Youth Activity Night', 'Social Groups', 'Salt Lake County', array['Salt Lake County']::text[], array['Youth']::text[], 'https://hosting.photobucket.com/images/i/lgbtqut/Logo_-_square.jpg', 'Youth Activity Night is a 10-14 age social group. We do a variety of activities, like game nights, craft nights, and speaker nights. An orientation is required.

Orientations can be completed from 3:00 pm-4:30 pm on Mondays, Tuesdays and Fridays.', 'utahpridecenter.org', '801-539-8800', 'youth@utahpridecenter.org', '1380 South Main, SLC, UT, 84115', null, null, true, null, null),
  ('iOFVtRWOSp21e21hCZ9wkw', 'Youth Futures (Ogden)', 'Homeless', 'Weber County', array['Weber County']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/5f2ad784e8fae48bcf796a04/5f663a8a013a6d5cde0ba425_Youth%20Futures.jpg', 'Youth Futures (Ogden) provides safe shelter, collaborative resources, respectful guidance and diverse support to homeless, unaccompanied, runaway and at-risk youth in Northern Utah. Youth Futures provides emergency shelter, temporary residence and supportive services for runaway, homeless, unaccompanied and at-risk youth ages 12-18. The shelter is open 24 hours per day.

Drop-In Services (6:30am-8:00pm - Everyday)

- 3 Hot Meals A Day (6:30am, 12pm, 5pm)
- Access to Hygiene, clothing, food, etc.
- Meet with a Case Manager
- Computer Stations
- Shower Services
- Laundry Services
- Transportation Assistance
- Therapy (Individual/Group/Family) 
- Life Skill Classes 
- Street Outreach: Youth Futures’ Street Outreach is conducted twice per week and provides outreach and crisis services on the streets to youth in Ogden', 'youthfuturesutah.org', '801-528-1214', 'info@yfut.org', '2760 Adams Ave Ogden, UT', null, null, true, null, null),
